Send an email to someone (rcp_gmail_send)
gmail · 3 steps · 1 pitfalls · platform · v3 · active
Difficulty: easy (Two calls and one check)
Use for: Send an email to a person by name or address
Tools: gmail.send_email
Related: gmail.create_draft

Steps
  1. gmail.search_contacts
     Find the recipient's address from the name.
     [risk read; idempotent]
  2. gmail.send_email
     Send the message to that address.
     [risk outward; needs your approval; auto key]
  3. gmail.create_draft (fallback for step 1: no contact matches)
     Save a draft and ask who it is for.
     [risk write; covered by your grant]

Pitfalls
  gmail.send_email
    - The account lacks the send scope. [http_403, ACCESS_TOKEN_SCOPE_INSUFFICIENT]
      Instead: Connect the account again with the send scope.

Evidence: 97% succeeded over 1000+ runs, at least 94% with 95% confidence in the last 30 days
Last eval: score 0.93, passed, 2026-10-15

signature: verified (platform, key plat-2026-10)
